  "steps": [
    "Start by cutting 200g low fat paneer into long slices.",
    "Heat a 1/2 tbsp ghee in a pan and pan-fry the slices until they’re golden brown on both sides.",
    "For the gravy, to a blender add 50g fried onions, 50g cashews, 50g yogurt and blend everything into a smooth paste.",
    "Now heat 1 tbsp ghee in a pan.",
    "Add 1 tsp cumin seeds, let it splutter.",
    "Add 200g tomato purée, 1 tsp ginger-garlic paste and cook for 2 minutes.",
    "Then add the prepared paste (from the blender), 1/2 tsp turmeric powder, 1 tsp red chilli powder, 1 tsp coriander powder, 1 tsp garam masala, 1 tsp salt.",
    "Mix everything well.",
    "Pour in 250ml water, let the gravy cook for 5 min.",
    "Now, add the paneer, 1 tsp kasuri methi, handful of coriander leaves and let everything cook for 2 mins. (If it’s too thick add more water)",
    "That’s it! it’s ready to serve."
  ],
